WEBVTT

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:32.490
New Year.

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:38.060
The Governor of Sashuu, Kou Shuurei, returned to the capital of Saiunkoku Kingdom, Kiyou,

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:44.530
where she spent some time together with her family, Shouka and Seiran.

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:53.100
From tomorrow onward, she will need to continue her efforts to make Sashuu into a place of learning.

00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:55.550
She can relax for now.

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:08.870
Another Governor of Sashuu, To Eigetsu, was working in Koren, the capital of Sashuu.

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:13.170
He worked hard day and night to fulfill his duties.

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:22.820
Hey, Eigetsu.

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:24.480
You must be happy.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:27.550
Promise me.

00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:31.360
Unless times are hard, you must smile as much as you can.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:41.600
You must never give up on life.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:45.490
Never look back. Keep moving forward.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:52.520
I will always love you, Eigetsu.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:57.900
Eigetsu-sama.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:02:58.980
Eigetsu-sama!

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:01.120
Oh, yes!

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:02.980
I'm sorry, Kourin-san.

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:04.900
I was daydreaming.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:08.070
Why don't you take a break?

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:10.500
You must be exhausted.

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:12.570
Not at all, I'm fine.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:15.360
You're so small, and yet so stubborn.

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:19.590
At least take a break.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.880
Thank you very much, Kourin-s-

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:29.850
Maybe I should have some tea too.

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:31.780
Ensei-san!

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:34.860
A-Are you still awake?

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:39.480
I'm his assistant. Since Governor-sama is awake, I can't afford to sleep.

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:41.110
Well, Eigetsu.

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:43.100
Why don't you take a break for today?

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:44.980
No thanks, I'm fine.

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:46.400
I can still work.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.130
Honestly, you're so stubborn.

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:52.910
Any way you cut it, you look like the youngest in your family, but you act like you're the oldest.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:55.160
Well, you're half right.

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:58.290
I was the youngest at first, but then I became an only child.

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:01.300
What do you mean?

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:03.030
Let me see...

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:07.390
My family ran out of provisions during the civil war,

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:08.940
and there was nothing they could do.

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:11.860
I had many siblings.

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:14.800
I was the youngest, and I was useless.

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:18.610
My family tried to abandon me,

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:24.110
but Doushu-sama from the palace happened to come by, and he took me in.

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:27.860
After that, he took me to Seika village.

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:30.590
I have been very fortunate ever since.

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:32.810
Eigetsu...

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:35.050
Please listen.

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:40.250
I'd like to share my story with you.

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:46.000
Doushu-sama was a person who loved to love things.

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:53.640
Even when a small bird chirped, or when a breeze shook the leaves, or when we ran out of rice...

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:57.040
Good for you, Eigetsu.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:00.140
Now we have an excuse to go out and find some vegetables on the mountain.

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.970
He was always happy, even when things like that happened.

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:02.970
Okay!

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:10.460
Except when I cried, I never saw his face without a smile.

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:13.060
He's just like you, Eigetsu-sama.

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:16.270
I'm nothing compared to him.

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:22.050
Doushu-sama loved two things more than anything else.

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:26.230
He loved people, and he loved life.

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:31.410
Say, Eigetsu.

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:33.910
Living is such a wonderful thing.

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:36.840
I was able to meet you, you see.

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:42.130
When I love someone, it warms my soul and makes me happy.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:44.300
Doushu-sama.

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:48.970
If someone else is happy, that makes me happy too.

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:52.660
I have decided to be happy until the day I die.

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:56.090
He was so unbelievably easygoing,

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:59.370
that many people took advantage of him.

00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:03.250
People took expensive medicine from him without paying.

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:04.470
But even then...

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:07.690
It'll be all right, Eigetsu.

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:11.840
More importantly, I hope this medicine helps them.

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:15.940
How could Doushu-sama survive, living like that?

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:20.790
It wasn't that he believed in the inherent goodness of people.

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:23.810
He knew that people could deceive and betray each other.

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:31.060
But he knew that people could be kind to each other, and trust each other.

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:35.790
He knew the reality of the world, but he still chose to love it regardless.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:40.410
I finally understood the meaning of "love" when I met him.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.080
Doushu-sama would always smile, even when he was deceived.

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:50.970
When his patients passed away, he would weep for days.

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:54.220
He was such a fine person.

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:58.860
Yes. He raised me to be who I am today.

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:02.310
That's why we have to be happy.

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:05.410
Ensei-san. Kourin-san.

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:08.450
When I left Seika, I made a promise.

00:07:08.920 --> 00:07:09.690
A promise?

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:15.870
Yes. I promised him that I would always smile, and live life to the fullest.

00:07:17.590 --> 00:07:19.750
Well then, I guess I'll keep working!

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:21.540
Wh-What do you mean?

00:07:22.230 --> 00:07:23.760
You should sleep for a while.

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:27.080
No, this is an opportunity to prepare for the government exam,

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:29.790
now that I've given up on becoming a doctor.

00:07:30.290 --> 00:07:31.880
I have to cover all my bases!

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:35.130
Well, why did you give up on becoming a doctor?

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:37.760
I haven't really given up,

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:42.150
but even if I become a doctor, I won't make much of a difference.

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:45.110
I realized that if I can get promoted in the civil service,

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:49.180
I might be able to reduce the amount of sadness in this world.

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:51.740
Yeah, that's right.

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:54.660
If your proposal succeeds...

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:58.100
What are you doing, Princess?

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:00.100
Are things going well?

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:09.750
I got approval from the Imperial General.

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:13.960
I'm so lucky that everything's been going smoothly so far this year.

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:16.000
Wait for me, Eigetsu-kun.

00:08:16.690 --> 00:08:19.380
At this rate, I'll be back in Sashuu soon.

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:21.520
But still...

00:08:22.130 --> 00:08:24.900
It's almost too good to be true.

00:08:25.550 --> 00:08:28.850
Both government branches agreed too easily.

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:31.870
They must be hiding something.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:42.580
Thank you very much for supporting her proposal to set up a research facility in Sashuu.

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:44.580
There's no need to thank me.

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:46.580
Shuurei is working hard.

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:51.170
But still, that's all thanks to your support.

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:53.790
I didn't do it for Shuurei.

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:58.630
I think it would be good for Sashuu's future.

00:08:59.210 --> 00:08:59.800
That's all.

00:09:03.490 --> 00:09:04.150
Shouka.

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:04.860
Yes?

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:09.670
I'm glad that Shuurei called me by name.

00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:15.810
But she'll be going back to Sashuu soon, won't she?

00:09:18.430 --> 00:09:21.740
I didn't want to help Shuurei.

00:09:22.930 --> 00:09:27.930
If things don't go well, she won't return to Sashuu for some time.

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:34.530
It's so lonely being an emperor.

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:38.860
I've gotten approval from most of the governors now.

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:43.290
All that's left is the Governor of Kokushuu, and the Departments of Civil Affairs and Treasury.

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:46.770
Yuushun-san and the others said that they'd handle the Department of Taxation, but...

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:47.890
I wonder how it went.

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:52.870
Oh.

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:59.050
This is the first time I've seen such unsung beauty.

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:03.030
It would be impossible to express it even in a painting.

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:03.910
Rin...

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:06.290
Yuushun, Sai Rin-dono.

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:09.140
I would like to congratulate you on getting married.

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:11.030
Thank you.

00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:13.920
Are you envious, Houju?

00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:15.370
Not really.

00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:21.350
Now then, I would like to talk about our work.

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:22.670
Keijirou.

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:28.640
I heard that you've found out how much it would cost to set up a research facility in Sashuu.

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:30.860
Yes, somehow.

00:10:30.860 --> 00:10:32.020
This is just an estimate.

00:10:32.430 --> 00:10:33.810
How much would it cost?

00:10:35.350 --> 00:10:38.830
Making a long story short, it would be very expensive.

00:10:39.640 --> 00:10:44.480
The governor's plan is intended to raise Sashuu's income.

00:10:45.650 --> 00:10:49.170
Once the project gets underway, it will generate revenue on its own.

00:10:49.590 --> 00:10:53.980
But the Treasury Department cannot afford to fund this venture.

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:58.320
As Minister, I can't allow this project to be paid for entirely with imperial capital.

00:10:58.320 --> 00:10:59.420
I suppose not.

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:02.610
But that's why I came all the way to Kiyou.

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:06.380
Kijin-dono. Do you know my profession?

00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:08.620
You're a member of the Merchants Guild.

00:11:11.130 --> 00:11:13.070
Can you really get them to approve of this project?

00:11:13.660 --> 00:11:17.510
No one knows exactly what it entails.

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:19.490
And how many years will it take for the project to make a profit.

00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:21.420
Don't underestimate me.

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:25.290
Business must be done with a long-term perspective.

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:30.590
People who lose sight of potential big gains by distracting themselves with the here-and-now

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:32.580
aren't allowed in the Merchants Guild.

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:37.600
It's just like governing.

00:11:38.330 --> 00:11:41.530
We need to look to the future, make a plan, and systematically follow through.

00:11:42.860 --> 00:11:50.310
But even so, if we need to invest all this money, it will not be easy to persuade the Merchants Guild.

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:52.310
Precisely.

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:55.310
That's why the governor of Kou has been working hard

00:11:55.570 --> 00:12:00.430
to gain government approval before we negotiate with the Merchants Guild.

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:03.330
It might be possible.

00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:10.430
If this project gets underway, it would be as though we'd found a golden goose that lasts forever.

00:12:10.900 --> 00:12:14.650
I'm sure that the Merchants Guild would be able to see the potential.

00:12:16.930 --> 00:12:18.440
Yes, exactly.

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:54.620
That's strange.

00:12:54.910 --> 00:12:57.950
How could the Minister of Civil Affairs disappear overnight?

00:12:58.280 --> 00:12:59.630
Did a ghost do this?

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:05.330
He looks like Kurou-sama, but...

00:13:05.990 --> 00:13:08.740
Okay... but why would he be here?

00:13:08.740 --> 00:13:09.970
It couldn't be! Is that a ghost?

00:13:10.530 --> 00:13:11.310
Kouyuu.

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:13.080
He really is Kurou-sama!

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:14.370
Where are you going?

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:17.110
Oh, I'm not going anywhere.

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:21.290
Why are you here, Kurou-sama?

00:13:21.290 --> 00:13:22.760
I came to see you.

00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:24.140
Have you made up your mind?

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:27.020
Th-That's easier said than done.

00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:30.870
If you waste time, someone else will steal Shuurei from you.

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:34.070
I'm not trying to force you to marry her.

00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:36.950
But if you want to rise higher than the civil service,

00:13:37.340 --> 00:13:38.700
joining the Kou family would help greatly.

00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:41.740
It would also benefit Shuurei.

00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:44.330
Shuurei wants to be promoted.

00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:48.660
No, she knows that she has to be promoted. It is her destiny.

00:13:49.740 --> 00:13:54.200
As far as I am concerned, if you marry Shuurei, you can use her family name.

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:55.710
You will become the heir to the Kou family.

00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:59.360
Shuurei will be promoted and gain control of the government.

00:13:59.630 --> 00:14:01.260
That way Shuurei would be at your side,

00:14:02.180 --> 00:14:05.030
and you'd kill three birds with one stone.

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:07.710
It is the best thing for both of you.

00:14:08.920 --> 00:14:12.220
You don't like most women, but you like Shuurei.

00:14:12.760 --> 00:14:14.540
Shuurei also likes you.

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:17.540
I don't care what kind of love it is.

00:14:18.010 --> 00:14:20.540
I think you would make a fine couple.

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:25.000
You would be good support for Shuurei.

00:14:26.490 --> 00:14:29.280
She could rise very far, the highest.

00:14:29.820 --> 00:14:31.890
You could raise her up above all.

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:36.940
Well, I'll give you some more time to think it over.

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:39.940
But you shouldn't take too much longer.

00:14:40.370 --> 00:14:43.080
Shuurei receives many marriage proposals every day.

00:14:43.510 --> 00:14:45.650
Ran Ryuuren sent one to her.

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:47.860
Ran Ryuuren.

00:14:52.210 --> 00:14:52.940
Yes.

00:14:53.420 --> 00:14:56.980
Shuurei is very special to Ran Ryuuren.

00:14:57.530 --> 00:14:59.160
The Ran family will not simply sit on their hands.

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:04.250
They are biding their time, but they will probably pursue her in earnest.

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:06.390
Consider my proposal carefully.

00:15:07.100 --> 00:15:12.110
I hope that you consider yourself the most suitable husband for Shuurei.

00:15:18.380 --> 00:15:20.770
Marrying Shuurei...

00:15:22.570 --> 00:15:26.440
If I do that, Shouka-san will become my father-in-law!

00:15:31.010 --> 00:15:34.620
If I do that, Reishin-sama will be Shuurei's father-in-law.

00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:40.700
I think Seiran would also tag along...

00:15:41.060 --> 00:15:45.590
Shuurei's husband must be determined and brave.

00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:51.640
I guess he does have determination going for him.

00:15:52.290 --> 00:15:53.530
E-Excuse me...

00:15:53.530 --> 00:15:54.550
Kouyuu-sama?

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:55.980
Are you all right?

00:15:58.650 --> 00:15:59.770
Sh-Shuurei!

00:16:00.190 --> 00:16:01.980
What happened, Kouyuu-sama?

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:05.020
Your face turned red, but then suddenly you were smiling.

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:06.580
Are you feeling ill?

00:16:06.580 --> 00:16:07.400
What?

00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:09.400
Did my face turn red?

00:16:09.930 --> 00:16:11.200
That's impossible.

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:13.400
Do you have a fever?

00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:14.690
I-I'm fine!

00:16:15.420 --> 00:16:18.230
Calm down! Calm down!

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:19.280
I'll be all right.

00:16:19.280 --> 00:16:21.240
Don't daydream.

00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:24.710
I need to calm down and talk to her casually.

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:28.070
H-Hi, Shuurei.

00:16:28.070 --> 00:16:29.700
Did you want something?

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:31.010
Um...

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:32.470
It's about Sashuu...

00:16:32.990 --> 00:16:35.480
Oh, that!

00:16:35.850 --> 00:16:38.540
I've obtained approval from the various departments.

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:38.540
Yeah.

00:16:38.860 --> 00:16:44.040
But the Minister of Civil Affairs kept saying he was too busy, so I haven't met with him yet.

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:45.730
That's right.

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:50.550
So, would you please notify him for me, Kouyuu-sama?

00:16:51.290 --> 00:16:53.610
Shuurei and me...

00:16:54.170 --> 00:16:55.120
A married couple...

00:16:56.820 --> 00:16:57.540
Excuse me...

00:16:59.440 --> 00:17:01.290
What am I thinking?!

00:17:01.990 --> 00:17:02.750
Kouyuu-sama!

00:17:03.110 --> 00:17:05.380
I've got to call a doctor! I'll call the royal physician!

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:09.780
Approval from the Minister of Civil Affairs? I'll get it right away.

00:17:10.370 --> 00:17:13.420
Oh, no. Just send a message to him on my behalf.

00:17:13.420 --> 00:17:14.920
I know he's busy.

00:17:15.440 --> 00:17:18.050
There is no way that person could be busy!

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:19.420
Is that so?

00:17:20.780 --> 00:17:24.570
If he isn't busy, why wouldn't he talk to me?

00:17:26.340 --> 00:17:27.740
How should I know?

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:31.430
A-Anyway, stay right here.

00:17:31.720 --> 00:17:32.530
I'll be right back!

00:17:34.050 --> 00:17:35.470
Kouyuu-sama! Where are you going?

00:17:35.470 --> 00:17:36.670
I'm going to see the Minister of Civil Affairs! Where else?

00:17:36.670 --> 00:17:37.940
The toilet's that way.

00:17:39.260 --> 00:17:41.120
That was just a warm-up!

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:46.380
Today he's acting very... strange.

00:17:48.780 --> 00:17:50.300
The real battle starts now.

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:55.810
Without money from the Merchants Guild, this proposal won't go through.

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:58.430
Yes, I know.

00:17:56.950 --> 00:17:58.430
Shuurei. Seconds please.

00:17:59.210 --> 00:18:02.560
Once we gather all the approvals we need, we can win over the Merchants Guild.

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:06.180
We'll capture our prey and go back to Sashuu.

00:18:06.760 --> 00:18:07.260
Yes.

00:18:10.250 --> 00:18:10.930
I'll do it.

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:14.670
Oh, thank you.

00:18:16.710 --> 00:18:19.790
So what's the status of the approval letters?

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:20.310
Rei.

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:24.650
Did you get approval from the Minister of Civil Affairs?

00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:27.230
Yes, Kouyuu-sama went.

00:18:30.110 --> 00:18:31.630
I told you to stay right here.

00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:34.260
I looked for you all over the place.

00:18:39.450 --> 00:18:41.240
I didn't move an inch.

00:18:41.450 --> 00:18:42.310
What did you say?

00:18:42.750 --> 00:18:46.610
If you didn't move, then what type of technique did you use?!

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:49.730
W-Well, never mind.

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:54.190
I got approval from the Minister of Civil Affairs for you to set up a research facility in Sashuu.

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:57.750
And I have a message from him as well.

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:00.280
He's got high hopes for it.

00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:04.920
Thank you so much, Kouyuu-sama.

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:08.580
Y-You should be thanking the Minister of Civil Affairs.

00:19:10.180 --> 00:19:12.710
So I got approval from the Minister of Civil Affairs.

00:19:13.240 --> 00:19:17.300
But why did Kouyuu-sama do something so nice for me?

00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:22.940
Anyway, I got approval from six government departments and five provincial governors.

00:19:23.530 --> 00:19:25.980
Governor Kai is traveling to Kiyou from Kokushuu province, but he'll be late.

00:19:26.300 --> 00:19:30.880
If I can get his approval, I'll have everything I need.

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:39.450
Governor Kai, due to the heavy snow, our arrival will be delayed by two or three days.

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:43.430
Is that so?

00:19:52.010 --> 00:19:59.240
I am truly grateful to you for being Eigetsu's guardian in my stead.

00:20:00.460 --> 00:20:02.240
My journey is over.

00:20:03.570 --> 00:20:04.470
It's over?

00:20:07.050 --> 00:20:09.650
I made a promise to Eigetsu.

00:20:10.390 --> 00:20:11.550
I'm glad I made it in time.

00:20:13.150 --> 00:20:13.960
What are these?

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:21.490
When you reach Kiyou, I would like you to give these to Kou Shuurei.

00:20:22.140 --> 00:20:23.740
To Kou Shuurei-dono?

00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:28.090
Eigetsu probably doesn't have much time left.

00:20:28.920 --> 00:20:34.550
So I would like to pass these, not to Eigetsu,

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:38.870
but to the Governor of Sashuu, who will understand our values.

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:43.280
The Governor of Sashuu.

00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:45.320
Kou Shuurei-dono.

00:20:46.710 --> 00:20:49.010
I wonder what she's like.

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:55.930
I was worried that Eigetsu would be left all alone again after leaving Seika.

00:20:56.700 --> 00:20:57.730
Now I can rest easy.

00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:01.380
Please convey this to Governor Kou.

00:21:02.360 --> 00:21:07.030
"Thank you from the bottom of my heart for not letting Eigetsu be alone.

00:21:08.170 --> 00:21:15.580
And... very soon, To Eigetsu will vanish from this world."

00:21:18.690 --> 00:21:19.590
Doushu-sama.

00:21:31.870 --> 00:21:33.010
Eigetsu.

00:21:34.360 --> 00:21:36.190
I kept my promise.

00:21:38.420 --> 00:21:39.920
I'm glad I made it in time.

00:21:42.320 --> 00:21:48.190
Meeting you, spending time with you, living with you...

00:21:49.230 --> 00:21:52.780
I was truly happy.

00:22:00.800 --> 00:22:04.080
I'll go on ahead and wait for you.

00:22:39.500 --> 00:22:40.680
Doushu-sama!

00:22:41.860 --> 00:22:42.870
Doushu-sama!

00:22:44.550 --> 00:22:45.920
Doushu-sama...

00:22:54.860 --> 00:22:57.560
Rest well, Doushu-sama.

00:22:59.190 --> 00:23:02.830
May you sleep soundly.

00:23:21.670 --> 00:23:25.440
We will meet soon, Kou Shuurei.

00:24:45.800 --> 00:24:48.250
I wonder if Eigetsu-kun is getting along with Kourin.

00:24:48.790 --> 00:24:49.710
I guess he doesn't have time for that.

00:24:49.990 --> 00:24:52.010
There's no time for Eigetsu or me to rest.

00:24:52.010 --> 00:24:54.540
We have to help make Sashuu prosperous.

00:24:54.940 --> 00:24:56.210
Huh? That sounds like a flute.

00:24:56.710 --> 00:24:57.390
Ryuuren?
